WEBVTT

00:04:28.417 --> 00:04:30.893
VV: No one has ever dived
the Southern Ocean before.

00:04:30.917 --> 00:04:32.226
I know why.

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:33.643
It's really, really hostile.

00:04:33.667 --> 00:04:34.976
The weather is awful.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.226
The word collision comes to mind.

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:39.101
But we did that one, yes.

00:04:39.125 --> 00:04:40.643
Glad that's over --
DB: Yeah --

00:04:40.667 --> 00:04:42.018
VV: Thank you.

00:04:42.042 --> 00:04:43.184
(Applause)

00:04:43.208 --> 00:04:45.101
DB: It's like you're racing through it.

00:04:45.125 --> 00:04:47.559
And now the Indian Ocean,
as Kelly mentioned.

00:04:47.583 --> 00:04:49.309
VV: Yeah, that was three weeks ago.

00:04:49.333 --> 00:04:51.934
We were fortunate enough
to actually solve the mystery.

00:04:51.958 --> 00:04:53.893
If someone had asked me three weeks ago,

00:04:53.917 --> 00:04:56.351
"What is the deepest point
in the Indian Ocean?" --

00:04:56.375 --> 00:04:57.643
no one really knew.

00:04:57.667 --> 00:04:58.976
There were two candidates,

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.643
one off of Western Australia
and one in the Java Trench.